,"k":"cafe","la":5.421308,"lo":100.339274,"d":732,"h":"Mo-Su 08:00-22:00","cu":"coffee_shop","wifi":1},{"n":"Salad Bowl","g":"food","k":"cafe","la":5.417305,"lo":100.338127,"d":764},{"n":"Antarabangsa Enterprise","g":"food","k":"bar","la":5.418671,"lo":100.3381,"d":767,"h":"Mo-Su 12:00-02:00"},{"n":"Thirty Three Stewart Houze","g":"food","k":"cafe","la":5.418967,"lo":100.338082,"d":773,"ph":"+60 12-299 3118","wifi":1},{"n":"Commune","g":"food","k":"cafe","la":5.413715,"lo":100.339276,"d":792,"cu":"coffee_shop","wifi":1},{"n":"Reggae Cafe","g":"food","k":"cafe","la":5.414637,"lo":100.338625,"d":798,"h":"Mo-Su 09:00-01:00","cu":"coffee_shop;breakfast;tea","wifi":1},{"n":"Queen Victoria Memorial Clock Tower","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.419384,"lo":100.344243,"d":175,"wp":"en:Queen Victoria Memorial, Penang","ds":"The Queen Victoria Memorial in George Town, Penang is a monument to Queen Victoria, begun after her death, located at the Penang Chinese Recreation Club. Penang's Victoria Memorial takes the form of a large piece of land known as \"Victoria Green,\" and a statue at the edge of Victoria Green at the junction of Burmah Road and Pangkor Road, the establishment of each being years apart from the other.","wpu":"Queen Victoria Memorial, Penang"},{"n":"Stage","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.420421,"lo":100.343841,"d":298},{"n":"Fort Cornwallis","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.420473,"lo":100.343868,"d":302,"h":"We-Mo 08:00-22:00; Tu 08:00-19:00","w":"https://mypenang.gov.my/culture-heritage/directory/399/?lg=en","ph":"016-411 0000","wp":"en:Fort Cornwallis","ds":"Fort Cornwallis is a bastion fort in George Town, Penang, Malaysia, built by the British East India Company in the late 18th century. Named after the then Lieutenant-General The 2nd Earl Cornwallis (1738–1805), the Governor-General of Bengal at the time of the fort's construction, it is the largest standing fort in Malaysia.","wpu":"Fort Cornwallis","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Fort_Cornwallis%2C_Penang_2023_01.jpg/960px-Fort_Cornwallis%2C_Penang_2023_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Chapel","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.420216,"lo":100.343228,"d":314},{"n":"Color Port","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.414833,"lo":100.343277,"d":400},{"n":"Sri Rambai Cannon","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.421328,"lo":100.343497,"d":405},{"n":"Penang 3D Trick Art Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":5.419759,"lo":100.341741,"d":410,"w":"https://3d.penangtrickart.com/"},{"n":"House of Yeap Chor Ee","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":5.41993,"lo":100.341802,"d":414},{"n":"Penang Ferry Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":5.414585,"lo":100.343495,"d":414},{"n":"Pinang Peranakan Mansion","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":5.417777,"lo":100.341172,"d":424,"h":"Mo-Su 09:30-17:00","w":"http://www.pinangperanakanmansion.com.my","ph":"+60-42642929","wp":"en:Pinang Peranakan Mansion","ds":"The Pinang Peranakan Mansion (Malay: Rumah Agam Peranakan Pulau Pinang) in George Town, Penang, Malaysia, is a museum dedicated to Penang's Peranakan heritage. The museum itself is housed within a distinctive green-hued mansion at Church Street, George Town, which once served as the residence and office of a 19th-century Chinese tycoon, Chung Keng Quee.","wpu":"Pinang Peranakan Mansion","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Pinang_Peranakan_Mansion_%28I%29.jpg/960px-Pinang_Peranakan_Mansion_%28I%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Wonderfood Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":5.416187,"lo":100.341256,"d":460,"h":"PH,Mo-Su 09:00-18:00","ph":"+6042519095"},{"n":"Chennai by wink","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":5.418636,"lo":100.340844,"d":465,"wifi":1},{"n":"PG Gold Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":5.41956,"lo":100.339951,"d":585},{"n":"Couzi Couji","g":"sights","k":"hostel","la":5.419004,"lo":100.339807,"d":585,"wifi":1},{"n":"Har Yang Sit Teik Tong Yeoh Kongsi","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.414909,"lo":100.340206,"d":632},{"n":"Little India","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.417183,"lo":100.339338,"d":633},{"n":"Penang State Art Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":5.421878,"lo":100.340497,"d":659},{"n":"James Richardson Logan Monument","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":5.42111,"lo":100.339828,"d":668,"w":"https://www.facebook.com/share/p/1EK7ysFzUr/","wp":"en:Logan Memorial","ds":"The Logan Memorial is situated in front of the Penang High Court at Light Street in George Town, Malaysia, and was erected in memory of James Richardson Logan, Scottish lawyer and man of letters, who lived in the Straits Settlements in the 19th century.","wpu":"Logan Memorial","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/20190823_Logan_Memorial-1.jpg/960px-20190823_Logan_Memorial-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lim Jetty","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.413056,"lo":100.340997,"d":706},{"n":"Goddess of Mercy Temple","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.418679,"lo":100.338572,"d":715,"wp":"en:Goddess of Mercy Temple","ds":"The Goddess of Mercy Temple (Chinese: 觀音亭; Pe̍h-ōe-jī: Koan-im-têng), also known as Kuan Im Teng or Kong Hock Keong, is a Mahayana Buddhist temple within George Town in the Malaysian state of Penang. Located at Pitt Street, it was built in 1800, making it the oldest Chinese temple in the state. The temple is dedicated to the Taoist deities and Buddhist Bodhisattva of Mercy, Guan Yin.","wpu":"Goddess of Mercy Temple","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Kong_Hock_Keong_Penang_Dec_2006_002.jpg/960px-Kong_Hock_Keong_Penang_Dec_2006_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cheap Beer Place","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":5.418702,"lo":100.338136,"d":763},{"n":"Penang State Museum and Art Gallery","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":5.4204